  "narrative": "These results mostly strengthen or contextualize the large accepted associations and add one new large mechanistic association, while leaving the KRAS/STK11 cluster uncertain. H57/R27 tests PTEN loss on STAT3 dependency within Avana screens: signed estimate +0.288 (95% CI +0.232 to +0.343), far above the approximate 0.025 absolute-scale threshold and excluding null in the hypothesis direction. I accept H57 and close it as a robustness stratum supporting H17. H58/R28 is the non-Avana complement: signed estimate +0.092 (95% CI -0.062 to +0.246), but only 27 exposed cells; it is promising in point estimate yet too imprecise to accept or reject. Thus the accepted PTEN/STAT3 association is robust in the major Avana stratum but library-conditional precision remains limited outside Avana.\n\nThe KRAS/STK11 follow-ups remain inconclusive. H62/R29 interaction estimate +0.022 (95% CI -0.024 to +0.067) is near the approximate clinical threshold in the expected direction but crosses null and includes both subthreshold and larger effects. H63/R30 complement KRAS-mutation effect in STK11-intact cells is small, +0.010 (95% CI -0.010 to +0.029), with only its upper end marginally approaching the threshold. H74/R38 reverse test, STK11 loss within KRAS-mutant cells, is +0.014 (95% CI -0.026 to +0.053). The pattern mildly favors a co-mutation-specific effect, but no individual comparison is decisive enough to accept a scientifically meaningful difference. I keep H62 and H74 active and defer H63.\n\nH64/R31 is too imprecise for PIK3CA-mutant context because only 38 cells contribute to one exposed subgroup: interaction estimate +0.001 (95% CI -0.150 to +0.152). I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than reject or interpret the null point estimate.\n\nThe specificity/context checks for the three largest accepted effects are decisive. H66/R32 shows that SMARCA4 loss predicts much stronger SMARCA2 dependency even among ARID1A-intact cells: +0.777 (95% CI +0.756 to +0.798). H67/R33 shows MSI-high predicts much stronger WRN dependency even among higher mutation-burden cells: +0.780 (95% CI +0.749 to +0.811). H68/R34 shows KEAP1 loss predicts weaker NFE2L2 dependency in the hypothesized direction even among STK11-loss cells: +0.775 (95% CI +0.727 to +0.823). These are far beyond the threshold, exclude null, and support that the global H5, H7, and H20 associations are not driven solely by the excluded co-alteration contexts. I accept and close each as informative robustness/context checks.\n\nFor the broad MAPK cross-pathway tests, H69/R35 tests BRAF V600E against weaker RIT1 dependency: signed estimate +0.004 (95% CI -0.025 to +0.033). The point estimate is negligible and the interval barely touches clinically meaningful positive values, so I leave it unresolved and defer. H70/R36 tests KRAS mutation against weaker EGFR dependency: signed estimate -0.010 (95% CI -0.027 to +0.008), opposite direction and below threshold; I reject it. H73/R37 is the strongest new discovery: TP53 loss in the hypothesized +1 direction gives +0.396 (95% CI +0.325 to +0.467). Because positive signed values correspond to higher, less negative USP7 dependency scores, this supports TP53-loss cells having weaker USP7 dependency relative to TP53-intact cells in this dataset. It is large, precise, and scientifically coherent with p53-pathway biology, but I treat it only as a dataset association. I accept H73, keep it active, and request independent validation because it is a new large association and validation would test whether it is reproducible outside this discovery partition rather than whether its discovery estimate is internally strong.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset associations now include: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H20 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; H17 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; H73 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency in hypothesized +1 direction. Robustness/context accepted and closed: H23/H24 SMARCA2 by library; H25/H43 WRN by Avana/high-Cas9; H26/H27 NFE2L2 by library; H66 SMARCA4 effect among ARID1A-intact; H67 MSI-high effect among higher mutation burden; H68 KEAP1-loss effect among STK11-loss; H57 PTEN/STAT3 robust in Avana. H58 non-Avana PTEN/STAT3 is active unresolved because exposed cell count is only 27 and interval is wide. H39 null ARID1A among SMARCA4-intact remains rejected. KRAS/STK11 cluster remains unresolved: H48 discovery +0.031 and validation +0.043; H62 interaction +0.022; H63 complement +0.010 deferred; H74 reverse +0.014. The pattern is suggestive but not accepted. H64 PIK3CA interaction is inconclusive and deferred due very small PIK3CA subgroup. H69 BRAF->RIT1 weak and deferred; H70 KRAS->EGFR rejected. H73 is requested for validation. Next priorities: (1) STAT3 PTEN-loss robustness by Cas9/lineage H59-H61; (2) KRAS/STK11 remaining active checks; (3) broader histology/complement subgroup tests for EGFR/KRAS/ERBB2/STAT3; (4) QC/demographic robustness for SMARCA2 and WRN H34-H42/H44-H47; (5) MYC expression/growth-rate refinements for POLR2A/RPL11 lower priority; (6) marker checks H19/H55/H56 and MDM2 context H54; (7) any new strong discovery from validation. All conclusions remain dataset associations unless independent validation and further robustness support general interpretation.",
